{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789821478,"nonce":"ev3cFEEr2ZDukxCRUM7Gac0DsdA=","message":"Zyntax reload landed in fd07f4b65647d1267ccded6003b76994d259f965: the loader records a module's file (registry::set_source) so the watch covers ZynML and Python modules, and Adapter::reload parses the module again (staged or from its file), hands the typed program to TieredRuntime::reload_typed_program (zyntax's own hot reload: functions diffed by name, changed code swapped behind cells, failures keep the old code) and publishes the interface again with the code now behind each symbol; the epoch bump refills the call sites as for Wren. Test: crates/caribou-interop/tests/reload_zyntax.rs (Point.area 12 -\u003e edit -\u003e 24 through the registry; a broken edit fails the reload and leaves 24; the Reload events carry both).\n\nLimits, tracked in 5bcf0d678e3b10197a5554df0fea80caaac84522e7921e6aabca4449011fdc98: the runtime diffs against the module it compiled last, so only a language's last-loaded module reloads (the adapter refuses the others by name), and a function an edit adds gets no function_ids entry. A module function another language holds as a value follows as well: `caribou::function::of_module` keeps the interface's (lang, module, name) and reads the callable again after the epoch moves, so Wren's `score` variable from `import \"game:tally\" for score` reaches the edited body (covered by the test).\n\nStill open here: Ash reload, the quiescent point with worker worlds, TypeDesc-level epochs if ever needed.","files":null}]}